      "text": "We start by letting $y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}$. We then substitute into the equation, which is now $y^2 + y = 12$. This quadratic equation can be solved by factoring, getting $(y+4)(y-3) = 0$. So $y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}$ must equal $-4$ or $3$. If $y = -4$, then $4x-16 = -12(x-4)$. Solving this gets $x= 0$. $x = 0$ is a valid solution, so it is the greatest value of $x$. If $y = 3$, then $4x-16 = 9(x-4)$. Solving this gets $x= \\boxed{24}$.).",
