      "text": "The given equation is\n\\[\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2+\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}=12,\\]so the common denominator is $3x-4$ and the equation becomes\n\\[\\frac{16x^2-64x+4(4x-16)}{(3x-4)^2}=12.\\]This simplifies to $x^2-8x+4=0.$  Using the quadratic formula, we find that the solutions are\n\\[\\frac{8\\pm\\sqrt{64-16}}{2}=\\frac{8\\pm4\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\]The greatest possible value of $x$ is $\\boxed{4+\\sqrt{3}}.$. The answer is 4+\\sqrt{3}",
