      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\(\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)=12\\), we start by letting \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). This substitution transforms the equation into a more manageable form:\n\\[ y^2 + y = 12. \\]\nWe can rearrange this equation to form a standard quadratic equation:\n\\[ y^2 + y - 12 = 0. \\]\nNext, we solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\\[ y = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}. \\]\nThis gives us two solutions for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = -4. \\]\nSo, we have \\( y = 3 \\) or \\( y = -4 \\).\n\nWe need to find the corresponding values of \\( x \\) from the expressions \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). First, consider \\( y = 3 \\):\n\\[ 3 = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}. \\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\) gives:\n\\[ 3(3x-4) = 4x-16. \\]\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\\[ 9x - 12 = 4x - 16, \\]\n\\[ 9x - 4x = -16 + 12, \\]\n\\[ 5x = -4, \\]\n\\[ x = -\\frac{4}{5}. \\]\n\nNext, consider \\( y = -4 \\):\n\\[ -4 = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}. \\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\) gives:\n\\[ -4(3x-4) = 4x-16, \\]\n\\[ -12x + 16 = 4x - 16, \\]\n\\[ -12x - 4x = -16 - 16, \\]\n\\[ -16x = -32, \\]\n\\[ x = 2. \\]\nSo, the possible values of \\( x \\) are \\( -\\frac{4}{5} \\) and \\( 2 \\). The greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\( 2 \\).\n\nTherefore, the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
